.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env

# WHY settings.local.json and not the whole .claude/ directory: everything else
# in there is the point of the D2 material and must ship - settings.json, both
# hooks, the slash command. This one file is per-machine state Claude Code writes
# and rewrites on its own, so tracking it would publish one contributor's local
# permission grants and then conflict with every reader's. It stays on disk,
# untracked, and Claude Code recreates it.
.claude/settings.local.json

# WHY these patterns when no such file exists in the tree today: that is the
# point. This repo ships a PreToolUse hook whose whole job is refusing to read
# credential files, and an ignore list that would happily commit one is a hole in
# the same argument. The cost of a pattern that never matches is nothing; the
# cost of the one time it would have matched is a rotated secret and a rewritten
# history.
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
**/.credentials.json
*.credentials.json

# WHY uv.lock is NOT ignored: it used to be, while the file was tracked anyway,
# so a clean clone would have silently lost it and resolved different versions
# than the ones every measurement in docs/status.md was taken against. For an
# application - and a study repo is one - the lock file is the reproducibility.
# Ignore it only in a library, where you want to test against a resolution range.

EXAM-FAQ.md
